inou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T00:28:27Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T00:28:27Z","body":"> That note is out of date as of 4.6\n\nI just tested this in 4.7.dev 7dac0bc3b and transparent (alpha blend) materials still don't show up in SSR:\n\n<img width=\"772\" height=\"574\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/75d7cf78-52da-4e5d-b596-4225a5aaeae2\" />\n\n**Testing project:** [test_ssr_transparent.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25114967/test_ssr_transparent.zip)\n\n> Is there a way to exclude an object from being reflected in SSR? For example, if I have a UI element that glows and I don't want to see it in reflections\n\nSee https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14075.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3857125460/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3860287414","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115541#issuecomment-3860287414","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115541","id":3860287414,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mF0-2","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T12:52:55Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T12:52:55Z","body":"this is because the reflection ray isn't hitting anything, but if there was a wall behind the alpha object, the pixel that has transparencies would show the transparency.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3860287414/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]